{"type":"Film","id":"FR2023_008","slug":"fr2023-008-l-envol","title":{"native":"L'Envol","english":"Scarlet"},"release":{"type":"Theatrical release","date":"2023-01-11","year":2023},"filmType":"Fiction film","directors":[{"id":"Pietro Marcello","slug":"pietro-marcello","name":"Pietro Marcello","birthYear":1976,"deathYear":0,"gender":"Male identifying","nationality":"Italy","awards":[]}],"genre":["Drama","Historical film (Heritage Film)"],"media":{"posterUrl":"https://medias.unifrance.org/medias/224/236/257248/format_page/scarlet.jpg","trailerUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xOSEffYJXNc"},"synopsis":{"native":"Quelque part dans le Nord de la France, Juliette grandit seule avec son père, Raphaël, un soldat rescapé de la première guerre mondiale. Passionnée par le chant et la musique, la jeune fille solitaire fait un été la rencontre d’une magicienne qui lui promet que des voiles écarlates viendront un jour l’emmener loin de son village. Juliette ne cessera jamais de croire en la prophétie.","english":"In northern France, Juliette grows up alone with her father, Raphaël, a veteran of the First World War. Passionate about singing and music, the lonely young girl meets a sorceress one summer who promises that scarlet sails will one day take her away from her village. Juliette never stops believing in the prophecy. Freely inspired by the tale \"The Scarlet Sails\" by Aleksandr Grin, Pietro Marcello's film blends music, history and folklore, bordering on magical realism."},"production":[{"country":"France","share":"Majority coproducer"},{"country":"Italy","share":"Minority coproducer"},{"country":"Germany","share":"Minority coproducer"}],"characters":[],"roles":[{"person":{"id":"Bernard Blancan","slug":"bernard-blancan","name":"Bernard Blancan","birthYear":1958,"deathYear":0,"gender":"Male identifying","nationality":"France","awards":[]},"role":"Minor actor/Cameo"},{"person":{"id":"François Négret","slug":"francois-negret","name":"François Négret","birthYear":1966,"de